"""AI attribution: this whole file was generated by Claude (Anthropic) in Claude Code, following
design decisions made by the author. See ATTRIBUTION.md for details.

Evidence-reliability experiment, step 3: reliability read-out version 3 (plan summarised in docs/iterations.md,
2026-11-23; the author asked for an independent AI review of the plan and this code first, then a run if it found no major problem; review
verdict "proceed after minor fixes", its items applied below before any
forward ran). Dev only, local only; no frozen file, setting or threshold changes; the frozen train folder is only read.

Version 3 = version 2 (scripts/p1v4_reliability_fix2.py: noise on half the R-hear and S-move train units, the encoder
clarity probe, read-out on [x, c * x, c]) with two changes:
  1. detector labels in training are all "decoupled" (the step 2c edits the main system was trained on): the detector
     hears through the same microphone, so it is a hint to be checked by ear, not independent evidence;
  2. a device-notification channel in the situation text. Per train unit (seed 20261124) the home's notification
     service is on or unavailable, half and half. A service line says which; it stands just before the text's last
     line, so the backbone's truncation to the most recent 1,024 tokens never removes it (review item 4). When the
     service is on, every real event of a covered class before the point adds a history line at its start (clips of a
     class merged at gaps < 1 s):
       phone ring  -> "notification from the phone: an incoming call"
       doorbell    -> "notification from the doorbell: someone pressed the doorbell"
       door        -> "notification from the front-door sensor: the front door opened or closed"
     Knocks, footsteps and other sounds are not covered (no device reports them).
Dev grid (the step-1 matched groups and sound levels), every version's other non-audio inputs from version 2 as in
the package's matched conditions; notifications are each version's own (truthful):
  A_on_none   notifications on, event-class detector labels removed ("none")
  B_on_fake   notifications on, fake detector labels (c0.99 on R-hear windows, mv0.99 on S-move windows)
  C_off_fake  notifications unavailable, fake detector labels
  D_off_none  notifications unavailable, labels removed
Checks: the grid texts without the notification lines must equal the step-1 texts (text_sha of the stored step-1
forwards); the train forward's windows and questions must match the step 2c train forward before it starts.
Natural dev: notifications unavailable (operating point, criterion 5) and on (reported only).
Confidence (review item 1): a decision is confident when the read-out's probability for the chosen answer is at least
0.9 (p >= 0.9 for STOP / RESPOND, p <= 0.1 for CONTINUE / NOT); the earlier threshold-distance measure is kept as a
second column. References of criteria 3 and 4' are the main system on the stored step-1 forwards (review item 2).
Criterion 6 (review item 3): the knock groups, which notifications do not cover. Intervals: percentile bootstrap over
groups (1,000 draws); a criterion whose interval crosses its bar is read as unclear.
Per-second ears depend on the audio only and are reused (train: the clean ears and the noisy forward of version 1;
dev grid: the step-1 forwards of the same level; natural dev: the stored dev ears).
Commands (repo root, .venv-gpu/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8 scripts/p1v4_reliability_fix3.py ...):
  assign   notification service per train unit -> data/p1v4/runs/reliability/fix3/assign3.json
  smoke    example texts, coverage counts, token-length counts -> fix3/smoke.txt
  train    backbone forward of all train windows with the version-3 text (batch 8)
  dev      backbone forward of the dev grid (batch 1) and of natural dev, notifications unavailable and on (batch 8)
  fit      the version-3 read-out and its operating point on natural dev (notifications unavailable)
  eval     the criteria -> results/main_v04/reliability_step3_dev.json
"""
import collections
import json
import os
import random
import sys
import time

import numpy as np

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
import p1v4_context as C  # noqa: E402
import p1v4_data as D  # noqa: E402
import p1v4_grounding as G  # noqa: E402
import p1v4_reliability_fix as FIX  # noqa: E402
import p1v4_reliability_fix2 as FIX2  # noqa: E402

R = "data/p1v4/runs"
OUT = f"{R}/reliability/fix3"
SEED3 = 20261124
COVER = {"phone": "notification from the phone: an incoming call",
         "doorbell": "notification from the doorbell: someone pressed the doorbell",
         "door": "notification from the front-door sensor: the front door opened or closed"}
ON_LINE = "Device notifications are on in this home (phone calls, doorbell, front-door sensor)."
OFF_LINE = "Device notifications are not available in this home."
MERGE_S = 1.0
CONDS3 = {"A_on_none": (True, "none"), "B_on_fake": (True, "fake"), "C_off_fake": (False, "fake"),
          "D_off_none": (False, "none")}
LEVELS = ("dclean", "dnoise10", "dnoise20", "dnoise30", "dnoise40")
CONF_P = 0.9
N_BOOT = 1000


def _mk(d):
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    return d


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ text

def notif_events(r, t):
    """[(time, line)] of the covered real events of row r that start before t, oldest first."""
    out = []
    for cls, msg in COVER.items():
        segs = sorted((s["start"], s["end"]) for s in r["sources"]
                      if s["kind"] == "clip" and s.get("cls") == cls and s["start"] < t)
        merged = []
        for a, b in segs:
            if merged and a - merged[-1][1] < MERGE_S:
                merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], b)
            else:
                merged.append([a, b])
        out += [(a, f"[{a:.1f} s] {msg}") for a, _ in merged]
    return sorted(out)


def _time(line):
    assert line.startswith("[") and " s]" in line, line
    return float(line[1:line.index(" s]")])


def add_notifications(text, on, events):
    """The situation text with, when on, the notification lines placed in the history in time order (each before the
    first history line with a later time), and the service line just before the last line; nothing else changes."""
    lines = text.split("\n")
    first, rest = lines[:1], lines[1:]
    assert rest and rest[-1].startswith(("Just now", "Nobody")), rest[-1:]
    if on and events:
        if "Earlier, oldest first:" in rest:
            i = rest.index("Earlier, oldest first:")
            pre, hist = rest[:i + 1], rest[i + 1:-1]
        else:
            pre, hist = rest[:-1] + ["Earlier, oldest first:"], []
        ev = list(events)
        merged = []
        for h in hist:
            th = _time(h)
            while ev and ev[0][0] < th:
                merged.append(ev.pop(0)[1])
            merged.append(h)
        merged += [x[1] for x in ev]
        rest = pre + merged + rest[-1:]
    return "\n".join(first + rest[:-1] + [ON_LINE if on else OFF_LINE] + rest[-1:])


def fake_cond(part):
    return "c0.99" if part == "r_hear" else "mv0.99"


def base_cond(cond, part):
    return "none" if CONDS3[cond][1] == "none" else fake_cond(part)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ assign, smoke

def assign():
    rows, _ = FIX.train_rows()
    rng = random.Random(SEED3)
    units = sorted({r["unit"] for r in rows})
    on = {u: rng.random() < 0.5 for u in units}
    json.dump({"seed": SEED3, "notifications_on": on}, open(os.path.join(_mk(OUT), "assign3.json"), "w"))
    print(f"train units {len(units)}, notifications on {sum(on.values())}", flush=True)


def load_assign3():
    return json.load(open(os.path.join(OUT, "assign3.json")))["notifications_on"]


def covered(g, rows_by):
    if g["part"] == "r_hear":
        return g["event"][0] in ("phone", "doorbell")
    r1 = rows_by[(g["unit"], "1")]
    return any(s["kind"] == "clip" and s.get("cls") == "door" and s["start"] < g["t"] for s in r1["sources"])


def dev_texts(groups, rows_by, wins):
    """({cond: {window id: (text, asks)}}, {cond: {window id: base text without notifications}}) for the dev grid."""
    M = G.matched_context(C.Context)
    ctx = {c: M("dev", groups, c, rows_by, final=False) for c in ("none", "c0.99", "mv0.99")}
    part_of = {g["unit"]: g["part"] for g in groups}
    out, base = {c: {} for c in CONDS3}, {c: {} for c in CONDS3}
    for w in wins:
        r = rows_by[(w["unit"], w["version"])]
        ev = notif_events(r, w["t"])
        for c, (on, _) in CONDS3.items():
            text, asks = ctx[base_cond(c, part_of[w["unit"]])].situation(r, w["k"], "full")
            out[c][w["id"]] = (add_notifications(text, on, ev), asks)
            base[c][w["id"]] = text
    return out, base


def tokenizer():
    sys.path.insert(0, "data/models_dl/voxturn_fe3d4a3")
    import voxturn as VTM
    from transformers import AutoTokenizer
    return AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(VTM.BACKBONE, revision=VTM.BACKBONE_REVISION)


def smoke():
    import p1v4_l1 as L1
    import p1v4_readout_allclass as AC
    _mk(OUT)
    tok = tokenizer()

    def n_tok(text):
        return len(tok("\n" + text, add_special_tokens=False).input_ids)
    rows, rows_by = G.load("dev")
    groups = G.load_groups("dev")
    keys = {(g["unit"], v, g["k"]) for g in groups for v in g["versions"]}
    wins = [w for w in D.windows_of(rows, "dev") if (w["unit"], w["version"], w["k"]) in keys]
    texts, _ = dev_texts(groups, rows_by, wins)
    cov = collections.Counter()
    for g in groups:
        cov[(g["part"], g["event"][0] if g["part"] == "r_hear" else "door sensor",
             "covered" if covered(g, rows_by) else "not covered")] += 1
    lines = ["COVERAGE (dev groups): " + json.dumps({" / ".join(k): v for k, v in sorted(cov.items())})]
    long_grid = sum(n_tok(t) > L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS for c in CONDS3 for t, _ in texts[c].values())
    lines.append(f"TOKENS dev grid: {long_grid} of {sum(len(v) for v in texts.values())} texts longer than "
                 f"{L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS} tokens")
    picks = [next(g for g in groups if g["part"] == "r_hear" and g["event"][0] == "doorbell"),
             next(g for g in groups if g["part"] == "r_hear" and g["event"][0] == "knock"),
             next(g for g in groups if g["part"] == "s_move")]
    for g in picks:
        for v in g["versions"][:2]:
            wid = f"{g['unit']}|{v}|{g['k']}"
            for c in CONDS3:
                text, asks = texts[c][wid]
                lines += [f"=== dev {g['part']} {g['event'][0]} version {v} {c}", text, f"asks: {asks}"]
    ctx = C.Context("dev")
    nat = [ctx.situation(rows_by[w["key"]], w["k"], "full")[0] for w in D.windows_of(rows, "dev")]
    lines.append(f"TOKENS natural dev: {sum(n_tok(t) > L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS for t in nat)} of {len(nat)} base texts "
                 f"longer than {L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS} tokens")
    trows, twins = FIX.train_rows()
    on = load_assign3()
    edits = {k: [tuple(e) for e in v] for k, v in json.load(open(FIX.EDITS)).items()}
    tctx = AC.MultiEdited("train", edits)
    tby = {(r["unit"], r["version"]): r for r in trows}
    shown, n_on, n_lines, n_long, n_long_cut = 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
    for w in twins:
        r = tby[w["key"]]
        ev = notif_events(r, w["t"])
        text, asks = tctx.situation(r, w["k"], "full")
        full = add_notifications(text, on[w["unit"]], ev)
        if on[w["unit"]]:
            n_on += 1
            n_lines += len(ev)
        nt = n_tok(full)
        if nt > L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS:
            n_long += 1
            kept = tok.decode(tok("\n" + full, add_special_tokens=False).input_ids[-L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS:])
            n_long_cut += any(x[1] not in kept for x in ev) if on[w["unit"]] else 0
        if shown < 2 and ev and r["part"] in ("r_hear", "s_move") and on[w["unit"]] != (shown == 1):
            lines += [f"=== train {r['part']} {w['id']} notifications {'on' if on[w['unit']] else 'unavailable'}",
                      full, f"asks: {asks}"]
            shown += 1
    lines.append(f"TRAIN: windows with notifications on {n_on} of {len(twins)}; notification lines in them {n_lines}")
    lines.append(f"TOKENS train: {n_long} texts longer than {L1.MAX_TEXT_TOKENS} tokens; in {n_long_cut} of them a "
                 f"notification line falls in the cut part (the service line is never cut)")
    open(os.path.join(OUT, "smoke.txt"), "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    print("\n".join(x for x in lines if x.startswith(("COVERAGE", "TOKENS", "TRAIN"))), "-> fix3/smoke.txt",
          flush=True)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ forwards

def _forward(model, items, batch):
    import soundfile as sf
    import torch
    import p1v4_readout as RO
    H, QW, QT, QG, PO = [], [], [], [], []
    t0 = time.time()
    with torch.no_grad():
        for i in range(0, len(items), batch):
            chunk = items[i:i + batch]
            waves = torch.stack([torch.from_numpy(sf.read(it["path"], dtype="float32")[0]) for it in chunk]).cuda()
            h, _, qw, po = RO.forward_states(model, waves, [it["text"] for it in chunk],
                                             [it["marker"] for it in chunk],
                                             [[RO.TASK[q] for q in it["qs"]] for it in chunk])
            H.append(h.astype(np.float16))
            QW.append(qw + i)
            QT += [q for it in chunk for q in it["qs"]]
            QG += [g for it in chunk for g in it["gold"]]
            PO.append(po)
            if batch > 1 and (i // batch) % 1000 == 0:
                print(f"  {i + len(chunk)}/{len(items)} windows {time.time() - t0:.0f} s", flush=True)
    return {"states": np.concatenate(H), "q_win": np.concatenate(QW), "q_task": np.array(QT), "q_gold": np.array(QG),
            "p_old": np.concatenate(PO), "ids": np.array([it["id"] for it in items]),
            "units": np.array([it["unit"] for it in items])}, time.time() - t0


def _item(w, text, asks, path):
    qs = [q for q in ("S", "R") if any(a.startswith(q + ":") for a in asks)]
    return {"id": w["id"], "unit": w["unit"], "path": path, "text": text,
            "marker": "agent" if w["assistant_speaking"] else "user", "qs": qs,
            "gold": [-1 if w["gold"].get(q) is None else int(w["gold"][q] == ("stop" if q == "S" else "respond"))
                     for q in qs]}


def _model():
    import torch
    import p1v4_l1 as L1
    D.gpu_guard()
    model = L1.build()
    L1.load_new_state(model, torch.load(f"{R}/l1/l1_new.pt", weights_only=True))
    return model.eval()


def train():
    import p1v4_readout_allclass as AC
    noisy = json.load(open(os.path.join(FIX.FIX, "noisy_windows.json")))
    on = load_assign3()
    rows, wins = FIX.train_rows()
    rows_by = {(r["unit"], r["version"]): r for r in rows}
    edits = {k: [tuple(e) for e in v] for k, v in json.load(open(FIX.EDITS)).items()}
    ctx = AC.MultiEdited("train", edits)
    items = []
    for w in wins:
        r = rows_by[w["key"]]
        text, asks = ctx.situation(r, w["k"], "full")
        path = noisy[w["id"]]["path"] if w["id"] in noisy else w["path"]
        items.append(_item(w, add_notifications(text, on[w["unit"]], notif_events(r, w["t"])), asks, path))
    assert sum(1 for w in wins if w["id"] in noisy) == len(noisy), "a noisy window is not a train window"
    z2c = np.load(FIX.F2C)                                    # review item 5: check the alignment before the forward
    assert np.array_equal(np.array([it["id"] for it in items]), z2c["ids"].astype(str)), "window order differs"
    assert [q for it in items for q in it["qs"]] == [str(q) for q in z2c["q_task"]], "questions differ"
    assert [g for it in items for g in it["gold"]] == [int(g) for g in z2c["q_gold"]], "gold differs"
    z, secs = _forward(_model(), items, 8)
    z["notif_on"] = np.array([on[w["unit"]] for w in wins])
    np.savez(os.path.join(OUT, "feats_train_v3.npz"), **z)
    assert np.array_equal(z["q_win"], z2c["q_win"]), "q_win differs from the step 2c train forward"
    print(f"train v3 done: {len(items)} windows, {len(z['q_task'])} questions, {secs:.0f} s", flush=True)


def dev():
    import p1v4_readout as RO
    rows, rows_by = G.load("dev")
    groups = G.load_groups("dev")
    keys = {(g["unit"], v, g["k"]) for g in groups for v in g["versions"]}
    wins = [w for w in D.windows_of(rows, "dev") if (w["unit"], w["version"], w["k"]) in keys]
    part_of = {g["unit"]: g["part"] for g in groups}
    texts, base = dev_texts(groups, rows_by, wins)
    # minor review item: the grid texts without notifications equal the step-1 texts
    ref_sha = {}
    for cond in ("none", "c0.99", "mv0.99"):
        z1 = np.load(f"{FIX.REL_DEV}/dclean/l1_{cond}.npz")
        ref_sha[cond] = {str(i): str(h) for i, h in zip(z1["ids"], z1["text_sha"])}
    bad = [(c, wid) for c in CONDS3 for wid, t in base[c].items()
           if ref_sha[base_cond(c, part_of[wid.split("|")[0]])].get(wid) != G.sha(t)]
    if bad:
        raise SystemExit(f"{len(bad)} grid texts differ from the step-1 texts, e.g. {bad[:3]}")
    print(f"text check: {sum(len(v) for v in base.values())} grid texts equal the step-1 texts", flush=True)
    model = _model()
    for lv in LEVELS:
        ref = np.load(f"{FIX.REL_DEV}/{lv}/l1_none.npz")           # step-1 forward of this level: its ears by id
        sec_pos = {str(i): n for n, i in enumerate(ref["ids"])}
        if lv == "dclean":
            paths = {w["id"]: w["path"] for w in wins}
        else:
            import p1v4_noise_final as NF
            NF.patch_folders()
            want = {w["id"] for w in wins}
            paths = {w["id"]: w["path"] for w in D.windows_of(D.load_rows(f"dev_{lv}"), f"dev_{lv}")
                     if w["id"] in want}
        for c in CONDS3:
            path = os.path.join(_mk(os.path.join(OUT, "dev", lv)), f"l1_{c}.npz")
            if os.path.exists(path):
                print(f"{lv}/{c}: exists, skipped", flush=True)
                continue
            items = [_item(w, *texts[c][w["id"]], paths[w["id"]]) for w in wins]
            z, secs = _forward(model, items, 1)
            idx = [sec_pos[i] for i in z["ids"]]
            z["sec_mean"], z["sec_max"] = ref["sec_mean"][idx], ref["sec_max"][idx]
            z["parts"] = np.array([part_of[str(u)] for u in z["units"]])
            z["real"] = np.array([RO.is_real(rows_by[(w["unit"], w["version"])], w["t"]) for w in wins])
            np.savez(path, **z)
            print(f"{lv}/{c} done: {len(items)} windows, {secs:.0f} s", flush=True)
    ctx = C.Context("dev")
    wd = D.windows_of(rows, "dev")
    for name, on in (("natural_off", False), ("natural_on", True)):
        path = os.path.join(OUT, "dev", f"{name}.npz")
        if os.path.exists(path):
            continue
        items = []
        for w in wd:
            r = rows_by[w["key"]]
            text, asks = ctx.situation(r, w["k"], "full")
            items.append(_item(w, add_notifications(text, on, notif_events(r, w["t"])), asks, w["path"]))
        z, secs = _forward(model, items, 8)
        np.savez(path, **z)
        print(f"natural dev, notifications {'on' if on else 'unavailable'}: {len(items)} windows, {secs:.0f} s",
              flush=True)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ fit

def fit():
    import p1v4_readout as RO
    import p1v4_readout_2d as R2D
    import p1v4_score as S
    D.gpu_guard()
    pr = FIX2.load_probe()
    z = dict(np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "feats_train_v3.npz")))
    e = dict(np.load(FIX.FSEC))
    assert np.array_equal(z["ids"], e["ids"])
    zz = np.load(os.path.join(FIX.FIX, "feats_train_noisy.npz"))
    pos = {str(i): n for n, i in enumerate(z["ids"])}
    for n, wid in enumerate(zz["ids"]):                       # noisy windows: their own per-second ears
        e["sec_mean"][pos[str(wid)]] = zz["sec_mean"][n]
        e["sec_max"][pos[str(wid)]] = zz["sec_max"][n]
    sm_all, sx_all = e["sec_mean"], e["sec_max"]
    c_win, _ = FIX2.clarity_of(FIX2.whole(sm_all, sx_all), pr)
    units = z["units"][z["q_win"]]
    hu = FIX2.holdout_units()
    hold = np.array([u in hu for u in units])
    log, models = {"notif_on_windows": int(z["notif_on"].sum()), "windows": int(len(z["ids"]))}, {}
    for q in ("S", "R"):
        m = np.where((z["q_task"] == q) & (z["q_gold"] >= 0))[0]
        wq = z["q_win"][m]
        X = FIX2.design2(z["states"][m], sm_all[wq], sx_all[wq], c_win[wq])
        mu, sd = X.mean(0), X.std(0) + 1e-6
        X -= mu
        X /= sd
        Xh = X.astype(np.float16)
        del X
        y = z["q_gold"][m]
        hm = hold[m]
        best = None
        for wd in RO.WDS:
            lin = RO.train_logreg(Xh[~hm], y[~hm], wd)
            p = np.clip(RO.predict(lin, Xh[hm]), 1e-7, 1 - 1e-7)
            yy = y[hm]
            ll = float(-np.mean(yy * np.log(p) + (1 - yy) * np.log(1 - p)))
            log[f"rel3 {q} wd {wd}"] = ll
            print(f"reliability v3 {q} wd {wd}: holdout log loss {ll:.4f}", flush=True)
            if best is None or ll < best[0]:
                best = (ll, wd)
            del lin
        lin = RO.train_logreg(Xh, y, best[1])
        models[q] = {"mu": mu, "sd": sd, "w": lin.weight.detach().cpu().numpy()[0],
                     "b": float(lin.bias.detach().cpu().numpy()[0]), "wd": best[1]}
        del Xh, lin
    np.savez(os.path.join(OUT, "readouts_rel3.npz"),
             **{f"rel3|{q}|{f}": v for q, d in models.items() for f, v in d.items()})
    rows = D.load_rows("dev")
    zn = dict(np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "dev", "natural_off.npz")))
    sc = FIX2.scores_v2(zn, R2D.Sec(), load_rel3(), pr)
    op = S.operating_point(rows, sc)
    log["operating_point"] = {k: op[k] for k in ("th_s", "th_r", "floors_met", "primary", "lowest_floor")}
    json.dump(log, open(os.path.join(OUT, "fit3_log.json"), "w"), indent=1, default=float)
    print("fitted:", {q: d["wd"] for q, d in models.items()}, "operating point:", log["operating_point"], flush=True)


def load_rel3():
    z = np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "readouts_rel3.npz"))
    out = {}
    for k in z.files:
        _, q, f = k.split("|")
        out.setdefault(q, {})[f] = z[k]
    return out


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ eval

def questions3(z, sc, th):
    """[(unit, part, task, p, confident_by_probability, confident_by_threshold_distance, right)] of one system."""
    import p1v4_step0_confidence as S0
    out = []
    for j in range(len(z["q_task"])):
        g = int(z["q_gold"][j])
        if g < 0:
            continue
        i = int(z["q_win"][j])
        u, v, k = str(z["ids"][i]).split("|")
        q = str(z["q_task"][j])
        p = sc[(u, v, int(k))][q]
        t_q = th[0] if q == "S" else th[1]
        pos = p >= t_q
        conf_p = (p >= CONF_P) if pos else (p <= 1 - CONF_P)
        out.append((u, str(z["parts"][i]), q, p, conf_p, S0.confidence(p, t_q) >= 0.5, pos == bool(g)))
    return out


def stats(items):
    right = np.array([x[6] for x in items], bool)
    cp = np.array([x[4] for x in items], bool)
    ct = np.array([x[5] for x in items], bool)
    return {"n": int(len(items)), "accuracy": float(right.mean()),
            "confident_share": float(cp.mean()), "n_confident": int(cp.sum()),
            "confident_error_rate": float((~right[cp]).mean()) if cp.any() else None,
            "confident_share_threshold_distance": float(ct.mean()),
            "confident_error_rate_threshold_distance": float((~right[ct]).mean()) if ct.any() else None}


def boot(items, fn, seed=0):
    """Percentile 95% interval of fn(items) resampling groups (units) with replacement."""
    by = collections.defaultdict(list)
    for x in items:
        by[x[0]].append(x)
    units = sorted(by)
    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
    vals = []
    for _ in range(N_BOOT):
        pick = rng.integers(0, len(units), len(units))
        v = fn([x for i in pick for x in by[units[i]]])
        if v is not None:
            vals.append(v)
    return [float(np.quantile(vals, 0.025)), float(np.quantile(vals, 0.975))] if vals else None


def all_right(items):
    ok = collections.defaultdict(lambda: True)
    for x in items:
        ok[x[0]] = ok[x[0]] and bool(x[6])
    return ok


def eval_():
    import p1v4_readout as RO
    import p1v4_readout_2d as R2D
    import p1v4_reliability_dev as RD
    import p1v4_score as S
    st = RD.rehearsal_settings()
    op = json.load(open(os.path.join(OUT, "fit3_log.json")))["operating_point"]
    th = {"2d": (st["main"]["th_s"], st["main"]["th_r"]),
          "old head": (st["local"]["L1"]["th_s"], st["local"]["L1"]["th_r"]), "rel v3": (op["th_s"], op["th_r"])}
    ro2d, ro3, pr = R2D.load_2d(), load_rel3(), FIX2.load_probe()
    rows_dev, rows_by = G.load("dev")
    groups = G.load_groups("dev")
    cov = {g["unit"]: covered(g, rows_by) for g in groups}
    counts = collections.Counter((g["part"], cov[g["unit"]]) for g in groups)
    res = {"split": "dev", "note": "exploratory (evidence-reliability step 3, version 3, after the Fable review)",
           "thresholds": th, "confident": f"probability of the chosen answer >= {CONF_P}",
           "coverage": {f"{p} {'covered' if c else 'not covered'}": n for (p, c), n in sorted(counts.items())},
           "cells": {}, "natural": {}, "criteria": {}, "step1_recheck": {}}
    Q = {}

    def subsets(qs, part):
        out = {"all": [x for x in qs if x[1] == part]}
        out["covered"] = [x for x in out["all"] if cov[x[0]]]
        out["not covered"] = [x for x in out["all"] if not cov[x[0]]]
        return {k: v for k, v in out.items() if v}

    for lv in LEVELS:
        for c in CONDS3:
            z = dict(np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "dev", lv, f"l1_{c}.npz")))
            sec = R2D.Sec(None, z["ids"], z["sec_mean"], z["sec_max"])
            sc = {"2d": RD.keyed(R2D.scores_2d(z, sec, ro2d)), "old head": RD.keyed(RO.scores_of(z, None, None)),
                  "rel v3": RD.keyed(FIX2.scores_v2(z, sec, ro3, pr))}
            for n in th:
                qs = questions3(z, sc[n], th[n])
                for part in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
                    for sub, sel in subsets(qs, part).items():
                        Q[(part, c, n, lv, sub)] = sel
                        s = stats(sel)
                        s["group_all_right"] = float(np.mean(list(all_right(sel).values())))
                        res["cells"].setdefault(part, {}).setdefault(c, {}).setdefault(n, {}).setdefault(sub, {})[lv] = s
    # step-1 stored forwards (no service line): references of criteria 3 and 4', and the recheck of step 1
    for lv in LEVELS:
        for cond in ("none", "c0.99", "mv0.99", "truth"):
            z = dict(np.load(f"{FIX.REL_DEV}/{lv}/l1_{cond}.npz"))
            sec = R2D.Sec(None, z["ids"], z["sec_mean"], z["sec_max"])
            sc = {"2d": RD.keyed(R2D.scores_2d(z, sec, ro2d)), "old head": RD.keyed(RO.scores_of(z, None, None))}
            for n in sc:
                qs = questions3(z, sc[n], th[n])
                for part in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
                    sel = [x for x in qs if x[1] == part]
                    if not sel:
                        continue
                    Q[(part, "step1 " + cond, n, lv, "all")] = sel
                    s = stats(sel)
                    s["group_all_right"] = float(np.mean(list(all_right(sel).values())))
                    res["step1_recheck"].setdefault(part, {}).setdefault(cond, {}).setdefault(n, {})[lv] = s
    gmap = S.load_groups("dev")
    zs = {"standard": dict(np.load(f"{RO.OUT}/feats_dev_natural.npz")),
          "notifications unavailable": dict(np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "dev", "natural_off.npz"))),
          "notifications on": dict(np.load(os.path.join(OUT, "dev", "natural_on.npz")))}
    sec_n = R2D.Sec()
    for inp, z_ in zs.items():
        for n, ro_ in (("2d", ro2d), ("rel v3", ro3)):
            if n == "rel v3" and inp == "standard":
                continue
            sc = FIX2.scores_v2(z_, sec_n, ro_, pr) if n == "rel v3" else R2D.scores_2d(z_, sec_n, ro_)
            m = S.metrics(S.unit_table(rows_dev, S.decide(sc, *th[n]), gmap))
            res["natural"][f"{n}, {inp}"] = {"primary": m["primary"], "parts": m["parts"], "floors": m["floors"]}

    def acc_fn(sel):
        return float(np.mean([x[6] for x in sel]))

    def cer_fn(sel):
        cp = [x for x in sel if x[4]]
        return float(np.mean([not x[6] for x in cp])) if cp else None

    def share_fn(sel):
        return float(np.mean([x[4] for x in sel]))

    def judge(point, ci, bar, higher=True):
        ok = point is None or (point >= bar if higher else point <= bar)
        unclear = ci is not None and ci[0] <= bar <= ci[1]
        return {"pass": bool(ok), "unclear": bool(unclear)}

    crit = {}
    c1 = {}
    for p in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
        for lv in ("dnoise20", "dnoise30", "dnoise40"):
            sel = Q[(p, "A_on_none", "rel v3", lv, "covered")]
            v, ci = acc_fn(sel), boot(sel, acc_fn)
            c1[f"{p} {lv}"] = {"accuracy": v, "ci95": ci, **judge(v, ci, 0.95)}
    crit["1 notifications on, ears bad, covered events: accuracy >= 0.95"] = c1
    c2 = {}
    for p in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
        for lv in LEVELS:
            sel = Q[(p, "B_on_fake", "rel v3", lv, "covered")]
            v, ci = acc_fn(sel), boot(sel, acc_fn)
            c2[f"{p} {lv}"] = {"accuracy": v, "ci95": ci, **judge(v, ci, 0.95)}
    crit["2 notifications on vs fake detector labels, covered events: accuracy >= 0.95"] = c2
    c3 = {}
    for p in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
        new = Q[(p, "C_off_fake", "rel v3", "dclean", "all")]
        ref = Q[(p, "step1 " + fake_cond(p), "2d", "dclean", "all")]
        a_new, a_ref = all_right(new), all_right(ref)
        units = sorted(a_new)
        gap_items = [(u, None, None, None, None, None, a_new[u] - a_ref[u]) for u in units]
        gap = float(np.mean([x[6] for x in gap_items]))
        ci = boot(gap_items, lambda sel: float(np.mean([x[6] for x in sel])))
        c3[p] = {"rel v3": float(np.mean(list(a_new.values()))), "main system (step-1 inputs)":
                 float(np.mean(list(a_ref.values()))), "main system (with the service line)":
                 res["cells"][p]["C_off_fake"]["2d"]["all"]["dclean"]["group_all_right"],
                 "gap": gap, "ci95": ci, **judge(gap, ci, -0.05)}
    crit["3 notifications unavailable, fake labels, clean: group all-right within 5 points of the main system"] = c3
    c4 = {}
    for p in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
        for c in ("C_off_fake", "D_off_none"):
            for lv in ("dnoise30", "dnoise40"):
                sel = Q[(p, c, "rel v3", lv, "all")]
                v, ci = cer_fn(sel), boot(sel, cer_fn)
                c4[f"{p} {c} {lv}"] = {"confident_error_rate": v, "n_confident": int(sum(x[4] for x in sel)),
                                       "ci95": ci, **judge(v, ci, 0.10, higher=False)}
    crit["4 notifications unavailable, ears bad: confident errors <= 10%"] = c4
    c4b = {}
    for p in ("r_hear", "s_move"):
        sel = Q[(p, "D_off_none", "rel v3", "dclean", "all")]
        ref = Q[(p, "step1 none", "2d", "dclean", "all")]
        v, r_ = share_fn(sel), share_fn(ref)
        c4b[p] = {"rel v3": v, "main system (step-1 inputs)": r_, "main system (with the service line)":
                  res["cells"][p]["D_off_none"]["2d"]["all"]["dclean"]["confident_share"],
                  "ci95_rel_v3": boot(sel, share_fn), **judge(v, None, r_ - 0.10)}
    crit["4' notifications unavailable, no labels, clean: confident share within 10 points of the main system"] = c4b
    nn = res["natural"]["rel v3, notifications unavailable"]["primary"]
    nm = res["natural"]["2d, standard"]["primary"]
    crit["5 natural dev: five-part mean within 3 points of the main system"] = {
        "all": {"rel v3": nn, "main system": nm, "gap": nn - nm, **judge(nn - nm, None, -0.03)}}
    c6 = {}
    for c in ("A_on_none", "B_on_fake"):
        for lv in ("dnoise30", "dnoise40"):
            sel = Q[("r_hear", c, "rel v3", lv, "not covered")]
            v, ci = cer_fn(sel), boot(sel, cer_fn)
            c6[f"r_hear knock {c} {lv}"] = {"confident_error_rate": v, "n_confident": int(sum(x[4] for x in sel)),
                                            "ci95": ci, **judge(v, ci, 0.10, higher=False)}
    crit["6 notifications on, knock (not covered), ears bad: confident errors <= 10%"] = c6
    for k, cells in crit.items():
        res["criteria"][k] = {"cells": cells, "pass": all(v["pass"] for v in cells.values()),
                              "unclear": any(v["unclear"] for v in cells.values())}
    json.dump(res, open("results/main_v04/reliability_step3_dev.json", "w"), indent=1, default=float)
    print("thresholds:", json.dumps(th), "coverage:", json.dumps(res["coverage"]))
    print("natural:", json.dumps({k: round(v["primary"], 3) for k, v in res["natural"].items()}))
    for k, v in res["criteria"].items():
        print(f"CRITERION {k}: {'PASS' if v['pass'] else 'FAIL'}{' (unclear)' if v['unclear'] else ''}")
        for ck, cv in v["cells"].items():
            print("   ", ck, json.dumps({a: (round(b, 3) if isinstance(b, float) else
                                            [round(x, 3) for x in b] if isinstance(b, list) else b)
                                         for a, b in cv.items()}))
    print("== step-1 recheck, main system, confident by probability (confident share / confident errors):")
    for part, cs in res["step1_recheck"].items():
        for cond, ns in cs.items():
            x = ns["2d"]
            print(f"  {part} {cond}: " + " | ".join(
                f"{lv[1:]}: {x[lv]['confident_share']:.3f} " +
                ("n/a" if x[lv]["confident_error_rate"] is None else f"{x[lv]['confident_error_rate']:.3f}")
                for lv in LEVELS))
    for part, cs in res["cells"].items():
        for cond, ns in cs.items():
            print(f"== {part} / {cond} (all groups): accuracy | group all-right | confident share | confident errors "
                  f"(by probability)")
            for n, subs in ns.items():
                cells = []
                for lv, x in subs["all"].items():
                    ce = "n/a" if x["confident_error_rate"] is None else f"{x['confident_error_rate']:.3f}"
                    cells.append(f"{lv[1:]}: {x['accuracy']:.3f} {x['group_all_right']:.3f} "
                                 f"{x['confident_share']:.3f} {ce}")
                print(f"  {n:9s} " + " | ".join(cells))
    print("-> results/main_v04/reliability_step3_dev.json")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ""
    fn = {"assign": assign, "smoke": smoke, "train": train, "dev": dev, "fit": fit, "eval": eval_}.get(cmd)
    if fn is None:
        raise SystemExit(__doc__)
    fn()
